course: dictionary
lesson: 367
title: Hard science words in health texts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look frightening, but you can often work them out from their parts and from the sentence. Antifungal has two parts: anti means against, and fungal is about fungi, which are living things such as mould. Put them together and you get something that works against fungi.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Ringworm is a fungus, not a worm, that makes a ring-shaped rash» tells you ringworm is not really a worm. Then «antifungal cream usually treats it» tells you the cream is used against the fungus that causes ringworm.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Try «antifungal cream usually stops the fungus» in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Antifungal means killing or stopping the growth of fungi.
fact: Fungi include mould and the fungus that causes athlete's foot.
fact: An antifungal is a medicine or cream that treats fungus infections.
fact: «Ringworm» is a fungus infection, not a worm, and it makes a red, ring-shaped rash.
fact: Ringworm can spread by skin contact and by shared mats and towels, and it can come from people or pets.
exercise: In «antifungal cream usually treats it», what does antifungal mean? | *Stops fungi from growing | Kills worms in the skin | Makes you feel sleepy | Cools a hot rash
exercise: Which of these is an antifungal? | *Athlete's foot cream | Sun hat | Sticking plaster | Bike helmet
exercise: According to «Ringworm ... spreads by skin contact, shared mats and towels», how can ringworm spread? | *By skin contact and shared towels | By eating too much sugar | By drinking dirty water | By being too cold
test: Is ringworm a worm, according to the lesson? | No, it is a kind of plant | Yes, but only in summer | *No, it is a fungus | Yes, it is a small worm under the skin
test: What does an antifungal stop? | The flow of blood | The growth of hair | *The growth of fungi, such as mould | The sound of a cough
exam: In «Ringworm ... can come from people or pets», what treatment does the sentence suggest? | *Antifungal cream | Vitamin tablets | Sunscreen | Bandage only
